{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Start the panel from the desktop menu as "Intel SST Audio", or run:

	sst-panel

Reading the driver's settings needs no privilege. CHANGING one does, because
the sysctls are root-writable only. The panel notices and shows a live
read-only view instead of refusing to start.

To change settings without running the whole panel as root, allow the sysctl
writes for a group - this grants exactly this driver's tree and nothing else:

	%wheel ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /sbin/sysctl dev.acpi_intel_sst.0.*

The Chinese translation needs a CJK font present, for example
x11-fonts/noto-sans-sc. Without one the text renders as empty boxes.
EOM
}
]
